# Lens Corrections

Lens corrections fix optical issues introduced by camera lenses: distortion (barrel/pincushion), vignette (darker corners), and chromatic aberration (color fringing).

Most editing software includes automatic lens correction that detects the lens and applies fixes. These are typically applied early in the post-processing workflow.

Related to [[Post-Processing]] and [[Photography Fundamentals]].
